<title>USA: ADT, Tyco antitrust waiting period expires.</title>
<headline>ADT, Tyco antitrust waiting period expires.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>ADT Ltd said on Monday that the Hart-Scott-Rodino antitrust waiting period for its proposed merger with Tyco International Ltd has expired with no action taken by regulators.</p>
<p>ADT, an electronics security firm, proposes to merge with Tyco rather than with Western Resources Inc. ADT on April 29 said it was soliciting proxies from its shareholders to oppose Western Resources' unsolicited proposal to replace the ADT board.</p>
<p>A special shareholders meeting was set for July 8. The company is based in Bermuda.</p>
</text>
